## 2. PROBLEM STATEMENT

During natural disasters such as floods and cyclones, emergency reports, affected-community requirements, available relief supplies, volunteers and relief operations are often managed through separate communication channels and organisations.

This fragmented approach can cause delays in identifying urgent needs, duplicate reports, inefficient resource distribution, unverified information, poor coordination and limited visibility into relief operations.

There is a need for a centralised and intelligent platform that connects affected communities with relief organisations and helps emergency coordinators make informed decisions.

The main challenge is not only the availability of resources but also the ability to identify, verify and deliver the right resources to the right people at the right time.

## 3. PROPOSED SOLUTION

CrisisWeave is an AI-powered disaster intelligence and relief coordination platform that connects citizens, NGOs, hospitals, volunteers and emergency coordinators through a unified digital ecosystem.

The platform uses AI to classify emergency reports, detect potential duplicates, identify priority cases and estimate short-term resource requirements.

Its cybersecurity layer supports secure access, evidence validation, suspicious activity detection and activity tracking.

An intelligent resource allocation engine recommends suitable relief supplies based on urgency, availability, quantity and geographical factors.

Interactive GIS maps, predictive analytics, Digital Twin scenario simulations and offline emergency reporting provide additional decision-support capabilities.

The complete process can be followed from emergency report submission to verification, resource allocation, dispatch and delivery confirmation.

