## 17. IMPORTANT SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

- Never store plaintext passwords.
- Never expose secret keys in frontend code.
- Use environment variables.
- Validate all inputs on the backend.
- Protect administrator routes.
- Restrict user access by role and resource ownership.
- Validate uploaded files.
- Restrict upload size.
- Use secure session settings.
- Apply rate limiting.
- Maintain audit logs for sensitive actions.
- Use database transactions for stock and allocation updates.
- Prevent duplicate offline submissions through idempotency keys.
- Do not trust values calculated only in the frontend.
- Do not expose private citizen details on public maps.

