## 19. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Build a working application, not just static UI mockups.
2. Connect the frontend to a real backend and database.
3. Use role-based authentication and protected routes.
4. Keep the code modular and easy to maintain.
5. Create reusable components.
6. Use realistic sample data for the demonstration.
7. Do not claim that simulated data is live disaster information.
8. Do not pretend an AI feature is functional if it only displays a hardcoded result.
9. Implement a simple working version before adding advanced models.
10. Ensure the main report-to-delivery workflow works end to end.
11. Provide clear setup instructions.
12. Test all user roles.
13. Keep the design professional and consistent.
14. Use meaningful error messages and loading states.
15. Never leave important buttons non-functional.

### Final instruction

Build CrisisWeave as a complete, professional, advanced hackathon prototype.

Prioritise functionality, usability, reliability and meaningful innovation over decorative UI.

The most important demonstration is the complete journey:

Emergency Report → AI Analysis → Trust Review → Incident Verification → Resource Optimisation → Coordinator Approval → Shipment → Delivery Confirmation.

The website should demonstrate how AI, cybersecurity and intelligent coordination can work together to improve disaster relief operations.